  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.047,
            0.419,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.132,
            0.621,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "BCDE is a rectangle (how?). Let us take its sidelengths to be height and base. Then,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.199,
            0.543,
            0.227
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_2.jpg",
          "content": "A r e a ( \\triangle A B C ) = \\frac { 1 } { 2 } \\times b a s e \\times h e i g h t"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.63,
            0.093,
            0.828,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.63,
                0.093,
                0.828,
                0.24
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.259,
            0.845,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since BXAE is a rectangle (how?), the height of the rectangle is the same as the height of the triangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.355,
            0.602,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, if the height and the base of a triangle are known, we can find its area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.409,
            0.557,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of a triangle "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " base × height."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.606,
            0.304,
            0.836,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.606,
                0.304,
                0.836,
                0.489
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.505,
            0.846,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Will this formula hold for the kind of triangle, around which we cannot draw a rectangle with BC as the base?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.38,
            0.569,
            0.594,
            0.73
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.38,
                0.569,
                0.594,
                0.73
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.738,
            0.846,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here is one way to look at it. The area of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the difference of the areas of ∆ADC and ∆ADB, each of which can be enclosed in a rectangle, as in Fig. 7.1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.323,
            0.797,
            0.697,
            0.888
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\begin{aligned} { { \\mathrm { A r e a } } \\; ( \\Delta { \\mathrm { A B C } } ) } & { { } = { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times h \\times { \\mathrm { D C } } - { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times h \\times { \\mathrm { D B } } } \\\\ { } & { { } = { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times h \\; ( { \\mathrm { D C } } - { \\mathrm { D B } } ) } \\\\ { } & { { } = { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times h \\times { \\mathrm { B C } } } \\end{aligned} }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.892,
            0.675,
            0.913
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the area formula holds for all types of triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.08,
            0.914,
            0.13,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "154"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
